## TECH STACK (v3.1)
Backend: Node.js + Express + Supabase (PostgreSQL) + express-rate-limit
Frontend: React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Vite + Framer Motion
Authentication: Supabase Auth (email/password)
Deployment: Vercel
Calendar: Internal Supabase tables (no Google Calendar dependency)
Real-time: WhatsApp Bot (Meta Graph API) + Webhook
Email: Nodemailer + SMTP
UI Components: Lucide React icons

## ARCHITECTURE (v3.8.0)
api/ contains all backend modules:
- api/index.ts - main API entry point (route definitions only)
- api/lib/shared.ts - shared utilities, constants, getClinicId(), getConfig()
- api/lib/booking.ts - booking engine logic (processBooking and helpers)
- api/lib/notifications.ts - email and WhatsApp notification sending
- api/lib/whatsapp.ts - WhatsApp state machine (runWhatsappStateMachine)
- api/lib/archive.ts - appointment archival logic
- api/cron/archive.ts - cron job entry point
- api/cron/reminders.ts - reminder cron job
Multi-tenant: clinic_id resolved via getClinicId() in api/lib/shared.ts
reads process.env.CLINIC_ID with 'beautiful-smile-demo' fallback for local dev
Message Templating: replaceTokens() helper in api/index.ts for {{PATIENT_NAME}}, {{CLINIC_NAME}}, {{APPOINTMENT_DATE}}, {{APPOINTMENT_TIME}}, {{CLINIC_ADDRESS}}, {{CLINIC_PHONE}} placeholders
NOTE: No server/ directory exists. Do not reference server/ paths.

## DATABASE SCHEMA (v3.6.3)
appointments: id, clinic_id, first_name, last_name, phone, phone_normalized, email, service, doctor_id, doctor_name, date, time, google_event_id (null), channel, status, notes, created_at
doctors: id, clinic_id, name, working_days, working_hours_start, working_hours_end, is_active, created_at
services: id, clinic_id, name, duration_minutes, description, price_range, is_active, created_at (DB-driven, replaces hardcoded BUSINESS_CONFIG.services)
blocked_slots: id, clinic_id, doctor_id, date, time_start, time_end, reason, created_at (entries with time_start=00:00 and time_end=23:59 and reason starting with 'Zi libera:' are auto-created by POST /api/holidays), group_id (nullable UUID)
clinic_config: id, clinic_id, key, value, updated_at (key-value store for editable clinic settings)
clinic_holidays: id, clinic_id, date, name, created_at (clinic closed days)
unlocked_slots: id, clinic_id TEXT NOT NULL, doctor_id, date, time, created_at
temp_reservations: id, clinic_id TEXT NOT NULL, doctor_id, date, time_start, time_end, created_at, expires_at (ephemeral slot pre-reservation)
reminder_log: id, appointment_id, clinic_id, created_at (prevents duplicate reminder sends)
clinic_users: id, auth_user_id (uuid FK auth.users), clinic_id, role, created_at
appointment_history: archive table with event_id (null in v3.0)

## CORE BOOKING ENGINE (v3.0)
processBooking() - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH, uses Supabase only
Steps:
1. sanitizePhone -> countActiveBookings(Supabase, phone_normalized) -> enforce MAX_ACTIVE_BOOKINGS
2. Resolve service -> durationMinutes
3. doctorId==='any' -> load balance | specific -> check internal availability
4. Slot availability checked against appointments + blocked_slots tables
5. Optimistic lock: INSERT Pending -> UNIQUE constraint catches duplicates
6. Success -> UPDATE to Confirmed (no Google Calendar sync needed)
7. Return {doctorName, doctorId, assignedMessage} (googleEventId: null, calendarId: null)

## INTERNAL CALENDAR ROUTES (v3.5.0)
GET /api/calendar/slots?date=YYYY-MM-DD&doctorId=dr1&durationMinutes=30
GET /api/calendar/appointments?date=YYYY-MM-DD&doctorId=dr1 (protected)
POST /api/calendar/block (protected) - block time intervals with optional groupId
DELETE /api/calendar/block/:id (protected) - unblock intervals
GET /api/calendar/blocks?groupId=UUID (protected) - fetch all slots in a vacation block

## DOCTORS MANAGEMENT ROUTES (v3.6.0)
GET /api/config - returns clinic config with doctors from Supabase (now reads from doctors table)
POST /api/doctors (protected) - create new doctor with auto-generated drN ID using recycling logic
PATCH /api/doctors/:id (protected) - update existing doctor with camelCase to snake_case field mapping
DELETE /api/doctors/:id (protected) - delete doctor after checking for future appointments (returns 409 conflict if found)

## SERVICES MANAGEMENT ROUTES (v3.6.1)
GET /api/services (protected) - list active services from DB
POST /api/services (protected) - create service with auto slug id
PATCH /api/services/:id (protected) - update service fields
DELETE /api/services/:id (protected) - delete service

## HOLIDAYS MANAGEMENT ROUTES (v3.6.1)
GET /api/holidays (protected) - list clinic holidays
POST /api/holidays (protected) - add holiday, 409 if date duplicate
DELETE /api/holidays/:id (protected) - remove holiday

## REMINDER SYSTEM ROUTES (v3.6.3)
GET /api/config/reminder (protected) - returns reminder configuration (lead hours and message template)
POST /api/cron/archive - protected by protectCron (x-cron-secret header), calls archiveDailyBookings()
POST /api/cron/reminders - protected by protectCron, requires reminder_sent_at column on appointments table
Scheduling: cron-job.org (NOT Vercel crons — removed from vercel.json)

## CALENDAR VIEW UI (v3.2.0)
Multi-view calendar: Day/Week/Month views with seamless switching (default: Week view)
Day view: Hourly grid (09:00-18:00) with doctor columns and real-time indicator
Week view: 7-day grid with appointment density indicators
Month view: Calendar grid with appointment counts per day
Features: Doctor filtering, navigation controls, clickable empty slots
All API calls protected by x-api-key header
Responsive design optimized for 1280px+ screens

## COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE (v3.2.0)
Modular component structure with proper separation of concerns:
- src/components/CalendarViews/DayView.tsx - Day calendar view component
- src/components/CalendarViews/WeekView.tsx - Week calendar view component  
- src/components/CalendarViews/MonthView.tsx - Month calendar view component
- src/components/AppointmentsList.tsx - Appointments list with filtering and pagination
- src/components/PatientsSection.tsx - Patient search and management
- src/components/SettingsSection.tsx - Clinic settings management (separate component imported by ClinicDashboard.tsx — future prompts touching Settings must explicitly specify THIS file, not just ClinicDashboard.tsx)
- src/components/BlockDoctorModal.tsx - Doctor time blocking modal
- src/ClinicDashboard.tsx - Main dashboard with state management and routing
All components use TypeScript interfaces and proper prop typing for type safety

## WHATSAPP STATE MACHINE
Endpoint: POST /api/webhook/whatsapp
Sessions: Supabase chat_sessions (timeout: WA_SESSION_TIMEOUT_MIN)
States: idle -> awaiting_service -> awaiting_doctor -> awaiting_date -> awaiting_time -> awaiting_full_name -> awaiting_phone_confirm -> awaiting_booking_phone_verification_code -> awaiting_cross_phone_input -> awaiting_cross_phone_otp -> confirming -> awaiting_email -> confirmed
Global interrupts: "meniu"/"start"/"restart", "operator"/"receptie", "anulare"/"cancel"
Cross-device cancel: SMS OTP verification flow with cross-phone verification
Test phone bypass: TEST_PHONE_NORMALIZED for MAX_ACTIVE_BOOKINGS only

## API RULES (v3.0)
All routes: try/catch, return JSON only
Admin routes: x-api-key required (protectRoute middleware)
Client errors -> Romanian, console.error -> English
Export: export default app (no app.listen() on Vercel)

## ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (v4.2.0)
Backend REQUIRED: SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, CLINIC_ID, CRON_SECRET
Frontend REQUIRED: VITE_SUPABASE_URL, VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, VITE_ADMIN_API_KEY
Backend OPTIONAL: CLINIC_TOTAL_DR_COUNT, CLINIC_ADDRESS, CLINIC_PHONE, DOCTOR_NAME_DR*, DOCTOR_WORKING_DAYS_DR*, DOCTOR_START_HOUR_DR*, DOCTOR_END_HOUR_DR*, MAX_BOOKING_HORIZON_MONTHS
Scheduling: MIN_LEAD_TIME_HOURS, CLINIC_TIMEZONE, SLOT_BUFFER_TODAY_MINUTES, NEXT_WORKING_DAYS_COUNT, MAX_DAY_SEARCH
Cache: DOCTOR_CACHE_TTL_MS
OTP: OTP_EXPIRY_MINUTES, OTP_CODE_LENGTH
Reminder: REMINDER_END_BUFFER_MINUTES, CRON_WINDOW_MINUTES
Security: PENDING_STALE_MINUTES
WhatsApp: WHATSAPP_GREETING_TEXT
Twilio: TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER (SMS), TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER (WhatsApp), TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL
REMOVED: GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON, CALENDAR_ID_DR* (v3.0 internal calendar), WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET, META_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN (v4.2.0 Twilio migration)
SECURITY: ADMIN_API_KEY=dv-secret-key-2026, CRON_SECRET (required for cron-job.org authentication)

## CODE STYLE (v3.2.0)
TypeScript only with strict mode enabled, async/await, ESM imports (.js extensions)
No hardcoded clinic data - use environment variables
Extract helpers for functions >40 lines
No magic numbers without constants
Component separation: Large components (>200 lines) must be split into separate files
Testing: All components should have corresponding test files in src/__tests__/
Type safety: All props must be properly typed with TypeScript interfaces
Code organization: Use proper folder structure (components/, hooks/, services/, types/)

## Validation & UX Rules (added v3.2)
- WebBot and WhatsApp time input handlers MUST validate slot availability before transitioning to confirmation state. If time not in available slots -> show error inline with list of available slots. Do NOT rely solely on processBooking() for this check.
- WhatsApp "time not found" must distinguish between: (a) unparseable input -> "Nu am recunoscut ora" and (b) valid format but unavailable -> "Ora nu este disponibil\u0103, alege\u021bi dintre: [...]"
- AddAppointment modal uses formErrors (Record<string, string>) for inline field-level validation. Errors shown as red border + text below field. Cleared on onChange.

## WHAT NEVER TO DO (v3.7.1)
- Render settings cards outside tab conditionals in SettingsSection — all cards must be inside their respective activeTab === '...' block
- Use alert() for user feedback in SettingsSection — use inline status state with auto-reset instead

## WHAT NEVER TO DO (v4.1.0)
- Expose VITE_ADMIN_API_KEY in frontend code or environment variables - use Supabase JWT authentication via getAuthHeaders()
- Skip x-api-key header for dashboard API calls - ALL fetch calls to /api/* MUST include header 'x-api-key': import.meta.env.VITE_ADMIN_API_KEY alongside the Authorization Bearer token
- Forget that Settings API calls live in SettingsSection.tsx (imported by ClinicDashboard) - getAuthHeaders() in SettingsSection.tsx must include 'x-api-key': import.meta.env.VITE_ADMIN_API_KEY
- Remove ADMIN_API_KEY from server environment variables - it remains server-only for internal/legacy use
- Touch /api/webhook/whatsapp or public WebBot routes with verifySupabaseJWT - these remain unprotected for public access
- Hardcode API secrets in browser bundle - never expose any API keys to the client side
- Set iframe.src in widget.js on page load — always lazy load (set src only on first button click)
- Add auth guard to /embed/chat route — must be publicly accessible without login
- Remove frame-ancestors * header from /embed/* routes in vercel.json — required for cross-site embedding
- Pass embedded=false (or omit) when rendering ChatWidget inside EmbedChatPage — always pass embedded=true
- Hardcode baseUrl in widget.js — always derive from document.currentScript.src
- Hardcode magic numbers — use parameterized constants from shared.ts (SLOT_BUFFER_TODAY_MINUTES, NEXT_WORKING_DAYS_COUNT, etc.)
- Hardcode timezone — use CLINIC_TIMEZONE env var (default Europe/Bucharest)
- Hardcode OTP parameters — use OTP_EXPIRY_MINUTES and OTP_CODE_LENGTH env vars
- Hardcode reminder buffer — use REMINDER_END_BUFFER_MINUTES env var
- Hardcode cron window — use CRON_WINDOW_MINUTES env var
- Hardcode clinic greeting text — use WHATSAPP_GREETING_TEXT env var
- Send reminder outside working hours — always use calculateReminderSendTime() which enforces workingHoursStart/End constraint
- Hardcode reminder template — always load from clinic_config.reminder_message_template with fallback default
- Return past slots for today's date in /api/calendar/slots — MUST filter by current Bucharest time + 60min buffer. Never use toISOString() for date comparison, use dayjs.tz() with BUCHAREST_TZ.
- Insert to reminder_log before confirming send success — only log after successful send
- Use BUSINESS_CONFIG.resources in WhatsApp handlers -- always use getCachedDoctors(clinicId) for live doctor list
- Upsert to clinic_config without clinic_id -- always include clinic_id and onConflict: 'clinic_id,key'
- Add holiday via POST /api/holidays without creating corresponding blocked_slots -- holidays must block all doctors
- Use Google Calendar API (removed in v3.0)
- Grant SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on any table to anon or authenticated roles -- all DB access must go through backend SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
- Add RLS policies that allow anon/authenticated direct table access -- backend handles all data operations
- Hardcode clinic data (names, phones, addresses)
- Duplicate processBooking() logic
- Expose stack traces in API responses (only in development)
- Use raw phone for DB lookups (use phone_normalized)
- Create appointments outside processBooking()
- Import local files without .js extension in api/
- Import server modules from api/ using ../server/ prefix (e.g., '../server/lib/shared.js')
- Use app.listen() on Vercel
- Call .map() directly on /api/calendar/slots response - it returns { date, doctorId, slots: string[] }, always use data.slots
- Add "Oricare medic disponibil" to the calendar header filter - that dropdown uses value="all" for all doctors, not value="any"
- Add new states to the WhatsApp state machine without a corresponding case handler in runWhatsappStateMachine()
- Ignore timezone handling in date parsing - always use BUCHAREST_TZ for Romanian dates
- Create components larger than 200 lines without splitting into separate files
- Disable TypeScript strict mode - all new code must pass strict compilation
- Skip unit tests for critical components like booking and calendar views
- Use SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in backend - always use SERVICE_ROLE_KEY for RLS bypass
- Return HTML error responses - always use JSON with proper error handling
- Skip phone normalization padding - use both exact and padded search strategies
- Disable global error handling middleware
- Send { id } to DELETE /api/delete-booking - endpoint requires { phone, date, time }
- Return weekend error message for invalid date formats — validate date existence BEFORE checking weekend
- Hardcode clinic address or phone — always use CLINIC_ADDRESS and CLINIC_PHONE env vars
- Send confirmation email without .ics attachment and clinic Google Maps link
- Run MAX_ACTIVE_BOOKINGS check only at booking end — check must also run at awaiting_phone_confirm state
- Use BUSINESS_CONFIG.resources for doctor list — now reads from Supabase doctors table via GET /api/config
- Open Add Appointment modal without creating ephemeral temp reservation -- always call createTempReservation in onSlotClick handlers
- Forget to release tempReservationId on modal close, appointment success, or conflict error -- must prevent orphaned reservations
- Skip the 10-minute client-side auto-release — temp reservations must expire to prevent permanent slot blocking
- Use blocked_slots table for temporary reservations — use dedicated temp_reservations table instead
- Use BUSINESS_CONFIG.services as source of truth — services now read from Supabase services table via getServicesFromDB() with hardcoded fallback
- Use hardcoded clinic profile fields — clinic name, phone, address, hours now read from clinic_config table via getClinicConfigFromDB() with env var fallback
- Insert to unlocked_slots or temp_reservations without clinic_id — always include clinic_id in all queries
- Hardcode 'beautiful-smile-demo' as clinic_id — always use getClinicId() from api/lib/shared.ts
- Insert to unlocked_slots or temp_reservations without clinic_id filter
- Query any table without clinic_id filter when multiple clinics may share the DB

